# APP_URL: The public URL this server is reachable at (e.g. your Netlify
# site URL, or http://localhost:3000 for local dev). Used to build the
# extension's server URL and to self-report from GET /api/info. If unset,
# the server derives it from the incoming request's Host header instead.
APP_URL=""

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DATABASE_URL — Supabase (or any standard Postgres) connection string
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Not set (default): the server stores data in local JSON/JSONL files
# under data/. Correct and fast for a single, long-lived Node process
# (`npm run dev` / `npm start` on a normal host) — but NOT safe for
# serverless deployments with more than one running instance (e.g.
# Netlify Functions), since each instance has its own filesystem.
#
# Set: the server uses server/pgdb.ts instead — a real Postgres database
# that every instance reads and writes identically, so dashboard counts
# never drift no matter how many function instances exist. This is
# REQUIRED for correct behavior on Netlify Functions.
#
# ── Setting this up with Supabase (recommended managed Postgres) ──
#
#   1. Create a project at https://supabase.com/dashboard (free tier
#      works fine for this app).
#   2. In the project, go to Project Settings -> Database.
#   3. Under "Connection string", choose the "Transaction pooler" tab
#      (recommended for serverless/Netlify -- uses port 6543 and handles
#      many short-lived connections correctly) and copy the URI. It
#      looks like:
#        postgresql://postgres.xxxxxxxxxxxx:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
#      (For a single long-lived process, e.g. running `npm start` on a
#      normal VM/container instead of serverless, the "Session pooler"
#      or direct connection on port 5432 also works fine.)
#   4. Replace [YOUR-PASSWORD] with your database password (set when the
#      project was created, or reset it on that same Database settings
#      page), and paste the full string below as DATABASE_URL.
#   5. That's it -- no manual schema/migration step. The server runs
#      `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS ...` for every table on first
#      connection, safe to run on every cold start, and it never drops
#      or truncates existing data.
#   6. TLS is handled automatically: server/pgdb.ts detects that this
#      isn't a localhost connection and connects with SSL enabled
#      (rejectUnauthorized: false -- the standard approach for connecting
#      to Supabase from Node, since its certificate chain doesn't always
#      validate against Node's default CA bundle).
#
# On Netlify: set this same value as an environment variable in Site
# settings -> Environment variables (not just in a local .env file) so
# the deployed functions can see it.
#
# Any other standard Postgres also works the same way (Neon, RDS, a
# self-hosted instance): just paste its connection string below.
#
# Example: postgresql://postgres.abcxyz:mypassword@aws-0-us-east-1.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres

DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.tfcxufkprwywemxyyeqd:Khan786%40cys%40%40%40%40%40%23%23%23%23%23%23@aws-0-ap-south-1.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres"
